Subject: [PATCH] MODCHECK: 1203 module presence check (EastSun ruling): first
 connect records every IO + motor module (ring / position / station / name;
 vacuum units and junctions excluded) into <dir of
 asGeneralPath>\Pci1203Modules.ini -- created only when absent (.tmp +
 no-replace rename, never overwritten; skipped when the scan is incomplete);
 afterwards read only: on every connect (boot + each link restore) within 10 s
 a listed module missing / not in OP / station changed, or an unlisted
 IO/motor module, raises ONE WAR16154 (ShowErrorMessage, same shape as
 WAR16152) per connect; silent while the link watch says lost.
 EtherCAT/Pci1203ModuleCheck.h (pure) + wb_serve EOF tick on the link-watch
 lines; ctest Pci1203ModuleCheck; no new vendor call (readonly gate passes)

